WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.510
Okay.

38
00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.810
At daybreak, the pirates will be landing
at this shore to begin their attack.

39
00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:03.350
But the only way that they'll be able
to get to the village is to go up this slope.

40
00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:07.110
The rest of the shoreline is sheer cliffs,
so they have to come through here.

41
00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.070
<b>The Slope</b>

42
00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:10.360
If we can fight them while they're
funneled into that narrow pass,

43
00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:13.070
their numbers won't mean anything
and the village will be protected.

44
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.660
Alright, sounds pretty easy.

45
00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:17.280
Talking about it is,
but victory depends on our strength.

46
00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.370
What is it that
you guys can do?

47
00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:20.240
I cut.

48
00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.160
I stretch.

49
00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.290
I steal.

50
00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.500
I hide.

51
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.380
Well, this time
you'd better fight!

52
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:28.670
Just making a funny.
C'mon, calm down!

53
00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.340
Ah, Klahadore.
Welcome back.

54
00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.630
How is she?

55
00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.180
She's resting just now.
She was quite exhausted.

56
00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.680
I leave town for a few hours
to tend to some errands,

57
00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.520
and everything falls to pieces.

58
00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.360
That Usopp certainly knows how
to cause trouble, doesn't he?

59
00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:48.270
Yes.

60
00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:52.530
And on top of everything else he's done
today, he claimed you were a pirate.

61
00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:55.030
Ha! I can't think
of a more outrageous lie!

62
00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.370
Indeed.

63
00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.540
What's this here?

64
00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.960
Well, that's
a present of course.

65
00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:09.500
From Miss Kaya
to you, Klahadore.

66
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.840
It's been three years
since you came to this mansion,

67
00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.720
and this gift is to say
thank you for your hard work.

68
00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.090
It's a commemoration of sorts.

69
00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.430
How nice.

70
00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.930
The glasses you're wearing are always
slipping and you have to push them back up.

71
00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.430
So, the lady of the house custom
ordered a new pair for you.

72
00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:27.020
Isn't she just the most thoughtful
young woman you've ever met?

73
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.820
How appropriate.

74
00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.440
Tomorrow will be a day
worth commemorating.

75
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:43.370
It's a crescent moon tonight.

76
00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:44.700
Huh?

77
00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:49.380
It's on nights
like these that I truly feel alive.

78
00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:52.630
My heart races, and my blood
boils in my veins.

79
00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.510
Ah!

80
00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.380
Klahadore,
what're you doing?!

81
00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:01.260
Why would you do such a thing
to Miss Kaya's present?

82
00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.720
Oh, I'll be receiving
a gift all right.

83
00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.430
But it won't be glasses.

84
00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:08.440
It'll be her entire estate.

85
00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:12.020
What're
you saying?!

86
00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:15.400
I suppose there's no reason
to carry on the act any longer.

87
00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:20.620
In a few hours, the village will be
mourning the unforeseen tragedy.

88
00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:27.250
Three long years
I've quietly waited for this.

89
00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:30.960
Miss! You have
to get out of here! Run!

90
00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.020
Captain Jango!

91
00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:54.770
Captain Jango, it's almost
daybreak, it's time get moving!

92
00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.360
Good morning, Captain.

93
00:04:58.360 --> 00:04:59.200
Good morning, sir.

94
00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:01.820
You idiots.

95
00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:04.780
Only the sun can wake me up
and live to tell about it.

96
00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.540
Do I make myself clear?

97
00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.040
He's in a really bad mood.

98
00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.000
Mornings are the worst.

99
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.210
Just look, the moon is still up,
so the sun couldn't have woken me.

100
00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.210
Now, which one of you did it?

101
00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.510
Our apologies, sir!
We're very sorry, sir!

102
00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.720
Good morning, gentlemen.

103
00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.390
Wait,
what's goin' on here?

104
00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:27.930
He was mad just
a second ago.

105
00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.520
So what? He's
in a better mood now

106
00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.890
and that's all that matters
so keep your big trap shut!

107
00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.160
Attention, men!

108
00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.900
<b>"One-Two" Jango
Acting Captain of the Black Cat Pirates</b>

109
00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:35.680
Let's set sail!

110
00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.700
Yep, I'm a genius.

111
00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:47.660
There's no way they'll be able
to make it up this slope now.

112
00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.660
All this oil we put here should keep them
occupied while we go to work on 'em.

113
00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:54.380
They're gonna be busy slipping and
sliding around like a bunch of idiots,

114
00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:57.380
then we show up and beat
the crap out of 'em!

115
00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.380
Wow, so that's
your plan, huh?

116
00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:00.340
That's right.

117
00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.930
I'm going to defend the village
no matter what it takes.

118
00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:06.180
Let's just hope none of us slip
on that oil and end up down there with them.

119
00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.930
Because that would be like
sliding into a meat grinder.

120
00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:12.850
Usopp, I gotta hand it to you,
you're pretty good at fighting dirty.

121
00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.270
Of course I am!

122
00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:17.150
There isn't anyone alive who
can best me with a sling shot,

123
00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.820
or beat me at the art
of fighting dirty!

124
00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:25.700
It's almost daybreak.

125
00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:27.140
They're coming.

126
00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.890
We're here!

127
00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:48.930
Alright, men!
You know what to do!

128
00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:52.520
Go ashore! Trash the village!
Head for the mansion!

129
00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:53.890
Aye, sir!

130
00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.650
Captain, there
are already two boats here!

131
00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:58.650
What?!

132
00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.070
Shall I investigate?

133
00:07:00.070 --> 00:07:01.320
Leave 'em for later.

134
00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:04.200
They don't look like treasure ships
to me and we have a schedule to keep.

135
00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.660
Where are they?

136
00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.160
I thought we
were gonna fight.

137
00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.330
The sun's up. What's the deal?

138
00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:14.120
Huh...
Maybe they over slept.

139
00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.960
Wait a minute.

140
00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:24.380
Maybe I'm hearing things, but it sounds
like battle cries from somewhere.

141
00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:32.060
Yeah, I definitely hear them.

142
00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:33.810
No, it can't be.

143
00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:35.640
What can't be?

144
00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.810
There's a shore just
like this to the north!

145
00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.560
They went...

146
00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.320
We're at the wrong shore?!
That's not good!

147
00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:47.610
Well, this is where they had
their secret meeting so I just assumed okay?!

148
00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:49.240
We need to hurry!

149
00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:51.830
Before they make it
to the village! Where is it?!

150
00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:53.620
You have to head
directly north from here.

151
00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.830
If you run you, could make it
in three minutes.

152
00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.620
The terrain there is almost
exactly the same,

153
00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.250
so all we need to do is stop
them at the slope.

154
00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:03.050
Oh no!

155
00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:07.010
If those filthy pirates are at the north shore,
then they've already seen our boats!

156
00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:08.430
They'll take our treasure!

157
00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.430
I'll be there in twenty seconds!

158
00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:11.800
Aw, man!

159
00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:15.140
My brilliant oil strategy
was all for nothing!

160
00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.980
My precious treasure...

161
00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:17.690
Hey!

162
00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:19.350
What're you doing?
Let's get outta here.

163
00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.310
Yeah.

164
00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:26.860
Help! I'm gonna fall!

165
00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.150
Let go, you moron!

166
00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.030
Sorry!

167
00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.370
Hello.

168
00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:32.910
See ya there!

169
00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:40.370
Sorry, but you understand,
the treasure's in danger.

170
00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:43.840
That oil won't be
a problem for you, right?!

171
00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:45.250
That girl's gonna pay!

172
00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.100
I swear on my life, they'll
never set foot in my village!

173
00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.100
That Luffy sure
is a good runner.

174
00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:58.350
He's so far ahead,
I can't even see him anymore.

175
00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:03.860
Run straight north!
Run straight north!

176
00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:07.490
Those mongrels are in big trouble if
they so much as look at my treasure!

177
00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.700
It's an ambush!
Somebody's up there!

178
00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.670
We meet again.

179
00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.850
I am the legendary Captain Usopp!

180
00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:38.180
I've been waiting for you!

181
00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.610
I wasn't supposed
to be the first one here.

182
00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:49.650
He was running way ahead of me.
I can't handle these guys alone.

183
00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:54.740
Crap!

184
00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:57.450
How am I supposed
to get past this stuff?!

185
00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.040
The village...
That can't be right.

186
00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:08.420
He said run north and I ran in a cold-ish direction
so I should be at the shore.

187
00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.430
It's you. I remember.

188
00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:18.350
You're one of the troublesome brats
who overheard our plan.

189
00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:19.680
What do you think
you're doing?

190
00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.060
I'm warning you!

191
00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:23.100
Leave here while you still can!

192
00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:27.860
If you don't, my 100 million crewmen
will massacre all of you!

193
00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:30.690
100 million?

194
00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:33.240
Are we really supposed
to believe that?

195
00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:36.410
No way! 100 million!
Incredible!

196
00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.330
Captain!
He's obviously lying!

197
00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:40.330
Then it's time
to call his bluff.

198
00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:41.750
They saw through it!

199
00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:44.620
That guy seriously
thought he could fool us.

200
00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.920
What's that?! You've been
lying to us this whole time?!

201
00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:49.800
Captain Jango,
take a look at this.

202
00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:50.840
Oh no, is it bad?

203
00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.010
No, sir! It's good!

204
00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.130
We searched those other ships
and found a huge load of treasure!

205
00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:58.470
It's hard to say how much, but I bet
it's around five million berries!

206
00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:00.310
What?

207
00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:02.680
Five million berries?

208
00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:06.150
How in the world did those guys get
ahold of so much treasure?

209
00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:09.770
I see
you found my loot!

210
00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:11.400
Well, you can have it!

211
00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:13.820
You're just gonna
let us take your treasure?

212
00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:15.700
That's right!

213
00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:19.580
Just turn around and forget all about
this place and the treasure is yours!

214
00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:22.290
I didn't think people
that stupid actually existed.

215
00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:26.330
At this point, he's just
embarrassing himself.

216
00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:29.210
Okay, do you know
what a pirate is?

217
00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:33.090
We're going to take this treasure and
there's nothing you can do about it.

218
00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:37.760
And there is no way we're turning
back until we get what we came for.

219
00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.470
Well, yeah, that makes sense.

220
00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:43.140
Alright, then.

221
00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:47.560
On the count of "one, two,
Jango," you'll let us by.

222
00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:49.400
It's that strange
weapon from before.

223
00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:52.150
One, two!

224
00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:52.690
Jan...!

225
00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:56.070
Don't you ever try to give
my hard-earned treasure away!

226
00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:01.240
My head!

227
00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.330
– Hey! Who is this crazy girl?!
– Captain!

228
00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.250
This isn't the time
to be hypnotizing yourself,

229
00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.290
we got a mission
to carry out, remember?!

230
00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:08.250
That treasure boat is mine

231
00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.250
and I'm not gonna let
you have a single berry.

232
00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.420
Do ya hear me? In fact
you better clear out,

233
00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.420
'cause I'm coming down
there to get it back!

234
00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.420
That really hurts!

235
00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:18.050
Who said you could
give them my treasure?!

236
00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:19.390
You got what you deserve!

237
00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:23.140
I didn't give them the treasure,
I just said I would give it to them!

238
00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:24.270
That's the same thing!

239
00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:26.640
And I just saved your life.

240
00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:31.110
I guess I forgot to mention it to ya
earlier, don't ever watch his ring routine.

241
00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:34.020
That weirdo's a hypnotist.

242
00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.650
Hypnotist?

243
00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:36.990
So, where's Luffy?

244
00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:39.820
He's a fast runner, I thought
he'd be here way ahead of you.

245
00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:43.620
I don't know. He either got lost
or he chickened out at the last minute.

246
00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:46.330
The only thing that
could keep him from a fight

247
00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:48.080
is getting lost.

248
00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:49.620
Right when we need him, too.

249
00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:51.380
I'll go ahead
and take command here.

250
00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:53.460
I think it's about time
you go 'n kick their butts!

251
00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.960
What?! Me?!
What about you?!

252
00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.340
I can't take on a boatload
of vicious pirates by myself!

253
00:12:58.340 --> 00:12:59.720
That's just suicide!

254
00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:01.470
What? Like I'm gonna do
any fighting?

255
00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:05.180
Beneath this calm exterior lies
the abject terror of a coward.

256
00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.970
Oh, so you think
you're scared?!

257
00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:09.940
Well, I'm so scared I am
literally about to cry!

258
00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:12.020
Please!
Your eyes are completely dry!

259
00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:13.150
You'll have to do
better than that.

260
00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:14.440
Liars can smell their own.

261
00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:16.190
That's just
your upper lip!

262
00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.190
I got beat up by...

263
00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:20.570
We don't have time
for this nonsense.

264
00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.280
Alright, men,
let's get to work!

265
00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.240
Crush them and move
to the village!

266
00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.620
Here they come.

267
00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.170
Wait! I know!
I have some caltrops!

268
00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.210
Those are just what
the doctor ordered!

269
00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:35.420
Lemme have some!

270
00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:40.260
You're gonna love this!

271
00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:41.220
Caltrop!

272
00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.220
Hell!

273
00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:56.770
Nami... if you're still alive when I get
outta here, I'm gonna kill you!

274
00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:06.660
Take that, oil!

275
00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:16.500
Now... how do I get
to the north shore from here?

276
00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:19.550
Run straight north!
Run straight north!

277
00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:21.720
Run straight nor...!

278
00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:28.810
But which way is north?

279
00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.400
Yes! We got 'em!

280
00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:38.520
Check it out! Here
comes... the Lead Star!

281
00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:42.320
Bastard!

282
00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:45.160
Way to go! You're
quite the warrior after all.

283
00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.370
Looks like you got this handled
so I'll just take a break.

284
00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:49.080
But you haven't done
anything yet!

285
00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:51.620
Uh, what is it?

286
00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.910
There are caltrops behind us.

287
00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:56.250
Idiot! You dropped
those things behind us, too?!

288
00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.590
Get outta the way!

289
00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:11.390
Ha. Don't tell me you really thought
you were going to stop us down there.

290
00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:17.270
Let's go, fellas!
Captain Kuro hates waiting!

291
00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:24.280
You again.

292
00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:27.570
Let go of me, you jackass!
You want some more?!

293
00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:30.330
Here! Have some!
Have a little more!

294
00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:36.580
I will never... let
you step foot in that village!

295
00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:40.790
All I did was lie
like I always do.

296
00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:44.470
See...

297
00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:47.300
Today will be like every other day
in that sleepy little town,

298
00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:50.260
'cause you and your cronies
will never set foot in it!

299
00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.180
Shut up!

300
00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:57.390
Stupid girl!

301
00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:02.770
Treasure...

302
00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:03.860
Are you...?

303
00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:08.030
Shut up! I won't
tell you again!

304
00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:12.450
We've wasted
enough time playing pirates!

305
00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:15.250
Quit bothering with them
and move to the village!

306
00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:18.330
Or have you forgotten
that this is Captain Kuro's operation?

307
00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:22.750
And he doesn't look favorably on his
well laid plans being ruined by idiots!

308
00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:24.170
He'll kill us all!

309
00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:25.960
You understand
that, you cretins?!

310
00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:26.720
He's right!

311
00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:28.550
Yeah! Let's get to the village!

312
00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:36.060
Don't go any further.

313
00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:38.310
I said stop!

314
00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.770
Turn back. Don't take
another step.

315
00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:42.020
Get off me!

316
00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.950
Please,
don't kill them.

317
00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:55.870
Just leave this village alone.
They're good people.

318
00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.290
They don't deserve this.
I love this place.

319
00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:01.420
Please!

320
00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:19.310
What is this,
Captain Jango?

321
00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:21.900
Nobody told us that killers
like those were gonna be here!

322
00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:24.400
It's about time.

323
00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:30.450
Is that the best
those pirates can dish out?

324
00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:33.870
Yeah, I was hopin'
for a challenge.

325
00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:34.530
And you!

326
00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:37.580
After leaving me down there, you're
lucky I'm not kickin' your butt too!

327
00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:39.410
Usopp, you big bonehead!

328
00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:42.040
You never told me
which direction was north!

329
00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.670
Who are these guys?

330
00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:53.680
They're late.

331
00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:57.220
I don't appreciate
tardiness. Not one bit.

332
00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:02.440
They know full well what happens to those
who are foolish enough to upset my plans.

333
00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:11.400
Do they think they
can take their sweet time?

334
00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.910
Well, if they have forgotten the
consequences of disappointing me...

335
00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:18.740
I'll kill them all.

336
00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:31.760
Wow.

337
00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:34.430
That was great. You guys
are really that strong?

338
00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:37.390
Mh-hm.

339
00:18:37.390 --> 00:18:40.680
Could you have been slower?
What took you so long?

340
00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.520
You're the one
who pushed me down

341
00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:44.390
that oil slick
so you could get out!

342
00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:47.360
It was an accident.
I slipped, you fell.

343
00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:48.860
At least one of us made
it outta there.

344
00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:51.650
That's better than both of us
being stuck at the bottom.

345
00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:53.700
It shoulda just been you!

346
00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:55.990
"Run straight north!" he says.
That's just great!

347
00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:59.530
I mean, how am I supposed to know
which way north even is out here, huh?

348
00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:03.290
Shut up. You're the one who ran away
so sure of yourself, ready to take on anyone.

349
00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:07.170
Well, I just got so excited,
I started running, you know?

350
00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:09.710
The sun rises high
in the sky now.

351
00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:13.300
And that means, Captain Kuro
grows very impatient.

352
00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:16.220
Men, don't just lie there.

353
00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:18.470
You can't tell me
you're going to let them win.

354
00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:20.470
They're just a couple of idiots.

355
00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:29.610
The fact, is we don't have time
to lollygag around here any longer.

356
00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:33.570
If our enemy is strong, then
we must become stronger than them.

357
00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.780
Here, stare deeply
into this ring.

358
00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:39.410
Now, I will count "one, two,
Jango" and after that,

359
00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:41.200
you will all begin
to grow stronger.

360
00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:44.200
Your wounds will heal and you
will grow stronger still.

361
00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:46.750
So, what is he doing?
It looks weird.

362
00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:48.210
Looks like hypnosis.

363
00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:50.590
He's trying to convince them
they're stronger than they are.

364
00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:52.170
Like that'll work.

365
00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.300
One... Two...

366
00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:56.260
Jango!

367
00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:01.140
No way.

368
00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:17.150
That one guy
completely destroyed the cliff!

369
00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:19.660
Now that's what I call power.

370
00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:22.620
I always thought hypnotizing people
was a buncha crap.

371
00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:23.910
That was just one of them.

372
00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:26.200
Imagine what
the whole crew can do.

373
00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:29.790
Now go!

374
00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:31.290
And strike down all
who stand in your way!

375
00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.390
Hey, you guys,
you might wanna move.

376
00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:48.020
Luffy. You and I will take
it from here.

377
00:20:51.190 --> 00:20:53.020
Alright then, what now?

378
00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.240
Uhh... Luffy?

379
00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:05.660
Don't tell me you let
that freak hypnotize you too!

380
00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.960
Ugh. He really is
a simple-minded idiot.

381
00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:17.300
Gum!

382
00:21:19.050 --> 00:21:21.550
Gum!

383
00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:26.060
Gatling!

384
00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:36.860
Damn you,
Captain Kuro.

385
00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:40.280
You made one hell
of a miscalculation.

386
00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:42.530
These are not your
average village idiots.

387
00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:04.550
Where's he going?

388
00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:08.390
What is he doing?

389
00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:20.740
That's right! Tear it down!

390
00:22:23.740 --> 00:22:25.620
Ah!
He's gonna destroy our ship!

391
00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:36.000
Oh no!

392
00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.630
He's gonna crush
us with it! Everybody run!

393
00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:42.510
Captain,
do something!

394
00:22:46.760 --> 00:22:48.760
One, two, Jango!
You will fall asleep!

395
00:22:51.270 --> 00:22:55.650
One, two, Jango!

396
00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:32.180
Looks like those guys are probably
down for the count, don't you think?

397
00:23:32.180 --> 00:23:33.220
I guess. Maybe.

398
00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:36.690
But Luffy's still
trapped underneath that cat.

399
00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:37.600
Just look.

400
00:23:38.190 --> 00:23:39.690
Relax. He's fine.

401
00:23:39.690 --> 00:23:43.360
You should really worry
about your own injuries by the looks of it.

402
00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:45.900
Damn that little brat.

403
00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:47.860
Now our whole plan's shot to hell.

404
00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:50.660
What am I gonna do
with this mess?

405
00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:55.290
Captain Kuro sees this
and he'll kill us!

406
00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:58.500
Butchie!
Come check this out!

407
00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:00.840
There's some bad stuff
going down.

408
00:24:00.840 --> 00:24:03.250
What the hell?!

409
00:24:03.250 --> 00:24:05.510
I forgot we still have
our trump card.

410
00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:08.890
Come forth,
Meowban Brothers!

411
00:24:20.860 --> 00:24:23.320
It looks like the butler
from Kaya's mansion.

412
00:24:23.320 --> 00:24:25.190
But it's so early
in the morning.

413
00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:27.400
Why is he walking
to the shore?

414
00:24:31.280 --> 00:24:38.140
As a kid I had a dream of a dazzling treasure

415
00:24:38.340 --> 00:24:45.160
I had a map in my head that I knew would lead me

416
00:24:45.410 --> 00:24:52.260
Charted a course all on my own so nobody would beat me

417
00:24:52.380 --> 00:24:59.520
The promised land was in my hand drew a line in the sand

418
00:25:02.220 --> 00:25:04.900
Look where I am

419
00:25:07.130 --> 00:25:13.310
My one ambitions slipping right through my hands

420
00:25:13.650 --> 00:25:20.580
But if the world ever changes Ill call out your name

421
00:25:20.740 --> 00:25:27.660
We could return to a time when our lives were still the same

422
00:25:27.790 --> 00:25:34.790
Take me to the place where memories remain

423
00:25:34.890 --> 00:25:40.660
Please dont ever let them fade
